# Context

## Why This Way
The exclusion mechanism is the point of the task. An earlier external
review argued a home-grown validator can silently misread unsupported
semantics; the corpus turns every unsupported case into a visible,
reason-carrying manifest entry, and the "keeps every skip justified"
test fails the moment an exclusion stops failing. Exclusions therefore
can only shrink through real fixes.

## Gotchas
- Upstream suite files keep their exact bytes; the directory is in
  .prettierignore so reformatting cannot blur provenance. The revision
  (1d82f70b, 2026-09-13) is pinned in manifest.json.
- The optional/ suite directory is deliberately not vendored: format
  assertion is opt-in by design in this validator, and the optional
  files target implementation-specific behavior.
- Updating the vendored revision requires re-triaging: new cases that
  fail need either a fix or a new manifest entry with a reason. The
  size guard makes a silent corpus shrink impossible.

